      content: 'Key areas to assess:\n- **Relapse history**: Number, type, and recovery from prior relapses. Time since last relapse. Current disease-modifying therapy (DMT) adherence and tolerability.\n- **Fatigue characterization**: Onset, severity, pattern (primary MS fatigue vs. secondary causes). Use the Modified Fatigue Impact Scale (MFIS) or Fatigue Severity Scale (FSS). Screen for depression (PHQ-9) and sleep disorders.\n- **Bladder/Bowel function**: Urgency, frequency, hesitancy, nocturia, incontinence, constipation. These are common early MS symptoms often underreported.\n- **Cognitive function**: Assess processing speed, attention, and memory. Consider Symbol Digit Modalities Test (SDMT).\n- **Mood and psychosocial**: Screening for depression and anxiety. Impact on work, relationships, and daily activities.\n- **Reproductive history**: Menstrual cycle, contraception use, desire for future pregnancy — critical for DMT counseling.\n- **Heat sensitivity**: Uhthoff phenomenon — does heat exposure worsen symptoms?\n- **Fall history**: Frequency, circumstances, injuries sustained, fear of falling.\n- **Spasticity symptoms**: Stiffness, spasms, especially nocturnal. Impact on gait and ADLs.',
