er delivery and discussing breastfeeding options.\'\n\n**5. Address breastfeeding and long-term concerns**:\n\'Exclusive breastfeeding may have some protective effect against postpartum relapses, though the data is still evolving. Some newer DMTs are considered compatible with breastfeeding. Your child\'s risk of developing MS is slightly higher than the general population — about 2-5% if one parent has MS compared to 0.1% baseline — but the vast majority of children of parents with MS do not develop the disease.\'\n\n**6. Empower and offer ongoing support**:\n\'This is not a decision you need to make today. I want you to know that many women with MS have healthy pregnancies and healthy babies. We will work together as a team to find the safest path for you and your future child. Would it be helpful to connect you with other women with MS who have navigated this journey?\'\n\n**Key principles demonstrated**: Empathy, normalizing her desire, evidence-based reassurance, structured planning, multidisciplinary coordination, patient empowerment.',
